# TATR @package_version@ alpha

Platform: @platform@. Built with @package_compiler@.
Runtime requirements: @runtime@.
Source revision: @SOURCE_REVISION@.
Source state: @SOURCE_STATE@. A working-tree package includes local packaging
changes beyond that commit and is for local review.

This is an experimental alpha. @platform_notes@
No universal Linux compatibility is claimed. macOS and other architectures are unverified.

Extract the entire archive. Run `bin/tatr --version` (Windows:
`.\bin\tatr.exe --version`), or add bin to PATH. Preserve both MIT notices under
share/tatr/licenses when redistributing. TATR itself needs no compiler or CMake;
the included demonstration deliberately uses CMake 3.25+ as its external program.

From the extracted package directory, with CMake on PATH:

```sh
./bin/tatr --file examples/tatr.toml list
./bin/tatr --file examples/tatr.toml plan hello
./bin/tatr --file examples/tatr.toml run hello
```

On Windows PowerShell use `.\bin\tatr.exe` for the executable above.
The example explicitly loads a public .env.example file, checks its value in a
CMake script, and writes TATR action records to stderr and logs/example-{date}.log.
Child output stays on the console. No private .env file is included or discovered.
The package directory must be writable for this example's log directory; adjust
logging.file.directory or remove its table when using a read-only installation.

TATR runs argument arrays or structured SMTP actions in dependency order, stopping
at the first task failure. Completion hooks can run after success or failure with
original-result context and an explicit warn/fail policy. Task cwd/env_file and log directory paths resolve from the TOML directory.
Use `--file` to select a config; there is no parent-directory discovery.
Exit codes: 0 success, 1 failed child, 2 CLI/configuration/runner/logging error.
There is no implicit shell, general command timeout, process-tree cleanup, parallel execution,
child-output capture or log rotation/retention. Log records omit argument arrays
and environment values, but task names/diagnostic paths can expose project metadata.

Additional public examples:

- examples/completion-hooks.toml and hook-summary.cmake demonstrate completion
  context after both successful and deliberately failed tasks (CMake required).
- examples/smtp.toml demonstrates SMTP tasks/hooks. Configure your server and
  addresses, copy .env.smtp.example to .env.smtp, and supply private credentials
  before sending. list/plan do not read credentials or contact the server.

SMTP requires an external native curl 8.0+ with SMTP/SMTPS and TLS support. It is
not bundled. TATR prepares UTF-8 plain-text MIME messages and requires verified
STARTTLS or implicit TLS; private CA bundles are supported. SMTP credentials use
private stdin, and SMTP client output is suppressed. Connection/send timeouts
(default 10/30 seconds) apply to curl transport only. Server acceptance does not
prove inbox delivery; no retries, spool, OAuth, HTML or attachments are included.
See the tagged docs/smtp.md for full settings, privacy and delivery limitations.

CHANGELOG.md describes this release. MANIFEST.json records the build and SHA-256
hashes of all payload files.
The release's SHA256SUMS file records the archive hashes.

Source and full documentation:
https://gitlab.com/wqyeo/thats-another-task-runner/-/tree/@package_version@
